<body>

    <h1>What is an API?</h1>

    <div class="section">
        <p><b>API (Application Programming Interface)</b> allows one software application to communicate with another.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>1️⃣ Types of APIs Based on Access</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><b>Open API (Public API)</b> – Available to everyone.</li>
            <li><b>Partner API</b> – Shared with business partners.</li>
            <li><b>Internal API (Private API)</b> – Used within an organization.</li>
            <li><b>Composite API</b> – Combines multiple APIs in one request.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h2>2️⃣ Types of APIs Based on Architecture</h2>

        <h3>REST API</h3>
        <p>Uses HTTP methods and JSON format.</p>
        <code>
GET /users<br>
POST /login
        </code>

        <h3>SOAP API</h3>
        <p>XML-based and uses strict standards.</p>

        <h3>GraphQL API</h3>
        <p>Client requests only required data.</p>
        <code>
query {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;user(id: 1) {<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;name<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;email<br>
&nbsp;&nbsp;}<br>
}
        </code>

        <h3>gRPC API</h3>
        <p>High-performance API using Protocol Buffers.</p>
    </div>

    <table>
        <tr>
            <th>API Type</th>
            <th>Style</th>
            <th>Use Case</th>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td>Open API</td>
